# A small causal model with an ontology header, used to demonstrate `rete reason`.
#
# Schema:
#   - Disease and Treatment are kinds of Factor (subClassOf chain → Factor).
#   - HealthyState owl:disjointWith DiseaseState (you can't be both).
#   - :causes is an owl:TransitiveProperty (causation chains compose).
#
# Two LAYERS of incoherence, one per tier of the coherence check:
#   - SCHEMA (Tier-0, `check_schema` / index-free): :Relapsed is rdfs:subClassOf
#     BOTH HealthyState and DiseaseState, which are owl:disjointWith → :Relapsed is
#     UNSATISFIABLE (no individual can ever be one), provable from the schema alone.
#   - INSTANCE (Tier-1/2, `rete reason`): patient :p is typed as both a HealthyState
#     and a DiseaseState → a disjoint-class clash on an actual individual.
# Plus a causal CYCLE  a → b → c → a  (find with SPARQL `?x :causes+ ?x`).

# --- schema -----------------------------------------------------------------
<http://ex/Disease> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://ex/Condition> .
<http://ex/Condition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://ex/Factor> .
<http://ex/Treatment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://ex/Factor> .
<http://ex/HealthyState> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith> <http://ex/DiseaseState> .
<http://ex/causes> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#TransitiveProperty> .

# --- unsatisfiable class (Tier-0): subclass of two disjoint classes ----------
<http://ex/Relapsed> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://ex/HealthyState> .
<http://ex/Relapsed> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://ex/DiseaseState> .

# --- causal cycle: a -> b -> c -> a -----------------------------------------
<http://ex/a> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ex/Disease> .
<http://ex/a> <http://ex/causes> <http://ex/b> .
<http://ex/b> <http://ex/causes> <http://ex/c> .
<http://ex/c> <http://ex/causes> <http://ex/a> .

# --- incoherent point: p is both Healthy and Diseased -----------------------
<http://ex/p> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ex/HealthyState> .
<http://ex/p> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://ex/DiseaseState> .
